      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-01-08T19:10:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "a mutex is heavy-weight and not zinger-friendly.\nI was hoping to do better.\nI\u0027m working on an improved implementation atomicity-wise,\nmight not fit in the current queue code, but that shouldn\u0027t be too bad to have an adhoc implementation here.\n\nThe big issue here is to implement the case where we need to discard previous entries because the log overflows.",
      "parentUuid": "ced64ddb_d13524f7",
      "revId": "71c313ab268dd5626e305fa2a38710495b43b9ce",
